1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:03,464
Honey Bunny Kidz presents:

2
00:00:03,464 --> 00:00:06,375
Pip and Mama Bunny's Rainy-Day Fort.

3
00:00:12,025 --> 00:00:14,825
Pitter, patter, pitter, patter.

4
00:00:15,175 --> 00:00:19,000
It was a rainy day at Honey Bunny's cosy house.

5
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:20,826
Oh, rain, rain.

6
00:00:20,826 --> 00:00:23,098
I wanted to play in the park today.

7
00:00:23,848 --> 00:00:25,039
Me too, Pip.

8
00:00:25,039 --> 00:00:27,023
What can we do inside?

9
00:00:27,773 --> 00:00:29,574
Hmm. I have an idea.

10
00:00:29,574 --> 00:00:32,548
Shall we build a cosy blanket fort?

11
00:00:33,298 --> 00:00:33,939
A fort?

12
00:00:33,939 --> 00:00:34,901
Yes, please!

13
00:00:34,901 --> 00:00:35,798
Woof, woof!

14
00:00:36,548 --> 00:00:39,298
What do you think we need to build a fort?

15
00:00:41,298 --> 00:00:42,996
We need two chairs,

16
00:00:42,996 --> 00:00:44,462
one big blanket,

17
00:00:44,462 --> 00:00:46,623
and lots of soft pillows!

18
00:00:49,273 --> 00:00:51,948
Pip and I found the pillows.

19
00:00:52,298 --> 00:00:54,873
How many pillows can you count?

20
00:00:56,873 --> 00:00:58,547
One, two, three, four!

21
00:00:58,547 --> 00:00:59,954
Four soft pillows!

22
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,978
What color is this pillow?

23
00:01:06,978 --> 00:01:09,403
Pink! Pink like my bow.

24
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,481
And this one is blue,

25
00:01:11,481 --> 00:01:12,699
this one is yellow,

26
00:01:12,699 --> 00:01:14,082
and this one is green.

27
00:01:16,732 --> 00:01:19,166
Mama Bunny held the chairs steady,

28
00:01:19,166 --> 00:01:21,205
and Honey and Pip spread the

29
00:01:21,205 --> 00:01:23,507
big purple blanket over the top.

30
00:01:24,257 --> 00:01:26,725
Grown-ups help with the chairs,

31
00:01:26,725 --> 00:01:28,757
so everything stays safe.

32
00:01:29,507 --> 00:01:31,628
Look! It's not just a fort.

33
00:01:31,978 --> 00:01:33,696
It looks like a ship!

34
00:01:34,446 --> 00:01:35,557
A pillow ship!

35
00:01:35,557 --> 00:01:38,041
Mama made a sail from an old sheet,

36
00:01:38,041 --> 00:01:39,871
and a broom for the mast.

37
00:01:40,621 --> 00:01:43,621
Mama folded a paper hat, too.

38
00:01:43,971 --> 00:01:46,721
Guess who wants to be the captain?

39
00:01:50,621 --> 00:01:51,882
Me! Captain Pip,

40
00:01:51,882 --> 00:01:53,010
ready to sail!

41
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:56,159
Captain Pip piled all four pillows

42
00:01:56,159 --> 00:01:57,910
on his side of the ship.

43
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,310
Pip, may I have a pillow too?

44
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:04,610
The floor is a little bit hard.

45
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,949
Hmm. But I like all the soft pillows.

46
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:11,024
What do you think Pip should do?

47
00:02:13,024 --> 00:02:13,608
I know!

48
00:02:13,608 --> 00:02:14,484
I can share.

49
00:02:14,484 --> 00:02:15,361
One for you,

50
00:02:15,361 --> 00:02:16,179
one for me,

51
00:02:16,179 --> 00:02:17,756
and two for our friends!

52
00:02:18,506 --> 00:02:19,704
Thank you, Pip!

53
00:02:19,704 --> 00:02:22,631
Sharing makes our ship cosy for everyone.

54
00:02:25,281 --> 00:02:26,281
Knock, knock!

55
00:02:26,681 --> 00:02:28,054
Who could that be?

56
00:02:28,054 --> 00:02:29,557
It's Dotty Duckling,

57
00:02:29,557 --> 00:02:32,106
with tiny raindrops on her feathers.

58
00:02:34,756 --> 00:02:37,002
Quack! Hello, friends!

59
00:02:37,002 --> 00:02:40,956
It's too rainy to swim in the pond today.

60
00:02:41,706 --> 00:02:42,924
Come aboard, Dotty!

61
00:02:42,924 --> 00:02:44,474
Here is a pillow for you.

62
00:02:45,224 --> 00:02:47,851
Thank you, Captain Pip!

63
00:02:47,851 --> 00:02:50,074
What a lovely ship.

64
00:02:50,824 --> 00:02:53,257
Everybody, row your arms with me!

65
00:02:53,607 --> 00:02:55,683
Can you row, row, row?

66
00:02:57,683 --> 00:02:58,737
Row and row,

67
00:02:58,737 --> 00:02:59,722
here we go,

68
00:02:59,722 --> 00:03:02,183
over the waves so soft and slow!

69
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:04,730
Rock to the left,

70
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:06,618
rock to the right,

71
00:03:06,618 --> 00:03:10,033
our pillow ship is snug and bright!

72
00:03:10,783 --> 00:03:13,283
Oh! Here comes a pretend wave!

73
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:15,374
Splish, splash!

74
00:03:16,974 --> 00:03:19,642
I love the pretend sea!

75
00:03:19,642 --> 00:03:22,824
What sound does a duck make?

76
00:03:24,824 --> 00:03:26,264
Quack, quack!

77
00:03:26,264 --> 00:03:27,524
You got it!

78
00:03:30,174 --> 00:03:32,842
Let's make looking circles with our hands,

79
00:03:32,842 --> 00:03:33,968
like a spyglass.

80
00:03:34,318 --> 00:03:36,238
Can you look through yours?

81
00:03:38,238 --> 00:03:39,294
I see, I see.

82
00:03:39,294 --> 00:03:40,020
Land ho!

83
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:41,341
It's Sofa Island!

84
00:03:42,091 --> 00:03:45,066
Hooray! Let's sail to Sofa Island!

85
00:03:45,816 --> 00:03:47,232
Row, row, row!

86
00:03:47,232 --> 00:03:49,066
We're almost there!

87
00:03:51,716 --> 00:03:55,141
Welcome to Sofa Island, sailors!

88
00:03:55,491 --> 00:03:58,691
I have apple slices for everyone.

89
00:03:59,441 --> 00:04:02,466
Pip shared the apple slices, too.

90
00:04:02,816 --> 00:04:03,980
One for Honey,

91
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:05,144
one for Dotty,

92
00:04:05,144 --> 00:04:06,240
one for Mama,

93
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,541
and one for Pip.

94
00:04:08,291 --> 00:04:09,800
Look out the window.

95
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:12,491
The rain is getting softer and softer.

96
00:04:13,241 --> 00:04:14,753
Let's take a big,

97
00:04:14,753 --> 00:04:16,341
slow ocean breath.

98
00:04:16,691 --> 00:04:17,830
Breathe in,

99
00:04:17,830 --> 00:04:19,866
like a wave coming in.

100
00:04:21,466 --> 00:04:22,912
And breathe out,

101
00:04:22,912 --> 00:04:24,816
like a wave going out.

102
00:04:25,166 --> 00:04:26,766
Whoosh.

103
00:04:28,366 --> 00:04:30,732
That was the best rainy day ever.

104
00:04:31,082 --> 00:04:34,162
Thank you for sharing the fort with me, friends!

105
00:04:34,912 --> 00:04:37,871
On a rainy day, a blanket, some pillows,

106
00:04:37,871 --> 00:04:41,312
and friends who share can make a big adventure.

107
00:04:42,062 --> 00:04:46,162
Share with a friend and subscribe to Honey Bunny Kidz!

108
00:04:46,762 --> 00:04:48,618
Bye-bye, little sailors!

109
00:04:48,618 --> 00:04:51,437
See you next time on Honey Bunny Kidz.
